index 0000000..233df01
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/wear-opus.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Optional packet Opus extension
+
+Base: SDK v0.2.0. Opt in with `platforms.gadget.extra.enable_opus: true`. The default is false. Missing ffmpeg/libopus or absent device offers keep PCM16 and omit the welcome extension. No native Python codec package is required. Do not enable on a running installation before review and device testing.
+
+Devices offer `formats: ["opus", "pcm16"]` in each 16 kHz mono mic/speaker capability. When enabled, `welcome.audio` selects `mic` and `speaker` separately. An absent selection means PCM16. Upload starts with `audio.start` format opus, rate 16000, frame_ms 20, id and stream. Before any packet, send `audio.codec` with stream and `opus_header`: Base64 RFC 7845 mono mapping-family-zero OpusHead. Android's unified AOPUS CSD must be unpacked; it is not a packet. Binary channel 1 frames carry one 20 ms packet (at most 1275 bytes), with ordinary stream/sequence framing. Missing headers, sequence gaps, wrong durations and limits reject the recording rather than sending damaged audio to STT.
+
+`audio.end` reconstructs CRC-protected Ogg pages and decodes through ffmpeg off the event loop into the existing mono 16 kHz PCM/WAV STT path. Limits are 60 seconds / 3000 packets, a bounded subprocess timeout, and no disk audio. Cancel discards the buffer. The optional output encoder consumes the existing resampled PCM pipeline, demuxes ffmpeg Ogg pages, sends `audio.start` with the RFC header, and sends paced raw packets. Provider Ogg bytes must never be treated as raw packets. No direct-provider Opus optimization is claimed in this patch. Android decodes at 48 kHz and plays through AudioTrack; codec delay comes from the header.
+
+Tests use real ffmpeg, malformed headers/packets, opt-in and extensions-off negotiation, unpaired rejection, sequence rejection, SDK WAV upload delivery, output framing and elapsed playback pacing. Stock protocol/audio unit tests run unchanged. Required hardware validation: Ultra encoder/decoder availability, Bluetooth throughput/latency, same utterances through PCM and Opus STT, audio quality, interruption and battery. Synthetic tones do not establish STT accuracy.
